  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "see",
      "title": "See it",
      "text": "The gold general moves one square straight in any direction, or one square diagonally forward, and takes the same way. It can't move diagonally backwards. It comes from shogi, Japanese chess, where it never promotes, and where the silver, knight, lance and pawn all promote to move like it. In shogi a captured piece also joins the side that took it and can be dropped back onto the board; this app doesn't play that rule. The marked squares are every square it can reach.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "g": "gold" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3G4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4"
    },
    {
      "kind": "try",
      "title": "Try it",
      "text": "Move the gold general to the marked square. It is diagonally behind it, so it takes two moves.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "g": "gold" }, "fen": "7k/8/8/8/3G4/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4",
      "targets": ["c3"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "read",
      "title": "Strategy",
      "pages": [
        {
          "text": "The gold general is a little stronger than the silver general, but still worth less than a knight or a bishop. It reaches six squares, all but the two diagonally behind it.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "g": "gold" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3G4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"], ["d4", "d3"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "The gold is the best guard of the king. Next to its king it covers the squares around it, and the two protect each other: here the gold guards g1 and the king guards g2. In shogi, players keep a gold or two beside their king for the whole game.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "g": "gold" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/8/8/6G1/6K1 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } }
        },
        {
          "text": "A gold can't step back diagonally. Here the black bishop attacks it from c3, behind it on the diagonal, and the gold can't take it back. It must step away.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "g": "gold" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3G4/2b5/8/7K w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"]]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "puzzles",
      "title": "Puzzles",
      "puzzles": [
        {
          "prompt": "Take the black gold general.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "g": "gold" }, "fen": "8/8/8/4K3/k7/1g6/G7/8 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "goal": { "kind": "capture", "square": "b3" },
